From 7f0557c16b4ee5ad56ad737e7ce037078b1564f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Cheng <chengyuejia@foxmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 02:11:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(quant): add KV cache quantization handlers for
 int4/nvfp4/fp8_e4m3/fp4_e2m1
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add Ascend NPU quantization handlers for new KV cache dtypes, integrating
with the existing @register_scheme / AscendAttentionScheme framework.

- kv_int4.py: INT4 per-token-head symmetric quantization handler
- kv_nvfp4.py: NVFP4 packed fp4 data + fp8 block scales handler
- kv_fp8_e4m3.py: FP8 E4M3 per-tensor quantization handler
- kv_fp4_e2m1.py: FP4 E2M1 microscaling format handler
- kv_cache_utils.py: Scheme dispatch and setup utility functions
- __init__.py: Export all new handler classes
- model_runner_v1.py: Call setup_kv_cache_quant after model loading

All handlers are no-ops at the apply() level — actual quantization
is delegated to the attention backend kernels.

Test commands run:
  python3 -m pytest tests/ut/quantization/test_kv_cache_quant.py -v --noconftest
All 35 tests passed.

Co-authored-by: Claude
Signed-off-by: vLLM-HUST <vllm-hust@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Paul Cheng <chengyuejia@foxmail.com>
